# Project terminology

Search `docs/lingo.md` for the relevant term if the file exists. Read only matching definitions and required command references. Treat the user's current explicit instruction as authoritative within host safety and permission boundaries.

An unmatched phrase does not automatically require a question. Use clear conversational context; ask only when plausible interpretations materially change the target, operation or risk. A glossary definition is not authorization for a destructive or external action.

Record a term only when requested or when a confirmed, recurring project-specific meaning will help future work. Create the file lazily when recording a real term. Include equivalent phrases, meaning, important prerequisites and the authoritative operational reference. Do not require boilerplate fields that add no information.

Complete the requested operation or explanation; dictionary maintenance must not become an unrelated precondition.
